Package: SubtypeR
Type: Package
Title: UCell-Based Single-Cell Molecular Subtype Assignment
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person(
        "csblab23",
        email = "csblab23@gmail.com",
        role = c("aut", "cre")
    )
Description:
    SubtypeR assigns a molecular subtype to every cell in a single-cell
    RNA-seq dataset using UCell gene-signature scoring, in the spirit of
    how CytoTRACE2 assigns a stemness score to every cell. Starting from a
    raw count matrix or an existing Seurat object, SubtypeR runs SCTransform
    normalization, retaining all genes rather than only variable features,
    scores a set of gene signatures per cell with UCell, and calls a
    single-cell subtype label using a per-signature quantile threshold.
    Two modes are supported: an "auto" mode with a built-in gene-signature
    panel for high-grade serous ovarian cancer (HGSOC), and a "manual" mode
    that accepts any user-supplied .gmt file, making the package applicable
    to any cancer type or custom set of gene signatures.
